@API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5244

### 1. Public endpoint. Works with no token.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/

### 2. The protected endpoint WITHOUT a token. Expect 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/weatherforecast

### 3. Log in. Saves the token for the requests below.
# @name login
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. The same endpoint WITH the token. Expect 200 and the forecast.
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/weatherforecast
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Wrong password. Expect 401.
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 6. ValidateToken on a real token. Expect isValid true.
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/auth/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{token}}"
}

### 7. ValidateToken on rubbish. Expect isValid false with a reason.
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/auth/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "not-a-real-token"
}
